{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787548164348089001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"convenient-rightist-flyingfish","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":8,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3f538986d91421f0e2f50b6d5e5b90d0f3bd7674aa88d2cdae97ed06d5ed4b72","event_uuid":"dd20981a-22c8-46a3-b392-8ed89f659f6c","position":{"commit_sha":"7470b7284eff42d798550ebc4abdee6954c074eb","position":"1787536885733823001-dd20981a-22c8-46a3-b392-8ed89f659f6c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2d8444a378bc53e8939fa023cb2258ffd6c119f75ad4e9867a42148f05708fd4","event_uuid":"dae3802c-b3ab-4d01-b2d5-215bca27c592","position":{"commit_sha":"ece97ed8197911f638b7a200c00b4ff38dce9161","position":"1787537074450531001-dae3802c-b3ab-4d01-b2d5-215bca27c592"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fc2492e0b72eb7989dd29abb362372788ef2f673f023e55efc85bcb4efd9bb40","event_uuid":"7d5e0bbd-e8fc-4c0a-bf63-39f278432907","position":{"commit_sha":"eb3622a9c0a2532d2b054484458499151e2fdf47","position":"1787537967247576001-7d5e0bbd-e8fc-4c0a-bf63-39f278432907"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"80fce390666b10a45879becfa38760ba8af2f46b594163cd830c64e408491205","event_uuid":"9f301206-75af-4db1-8594-578c28cf8a95","position":{"commit_sha":"36be95cecf90e8624d057fbf1f0c57f29c3908ed","position":"1787538043603955001-9f301206-75af-4db1-8594-578c28cf8a95"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"06a29a8a14db2ae833e611ee4248ff86c513adf9faff34d4cd3f605e8ce0e489","event_uuid":"bc900acc-24fc-43db-9400-3a89c7a395e9","position":{"commit_sha":"1c722889604c05d3eb3ef6199a6e4dbcc3376675","position":"1787541837887253001-bc900acc-24fc-43db-9400-3a89c7a395e9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"95c1ea6df16f102c4b8ce599254c27385bcf1866390ffa60be2344a9fc93804c","event_uuid":"dce138f6-6231-4650-8f7c-74ba36825e16","position":{"commit_sha":"07d851cc203add599b241e7368e4a531f78467d3","position":"1787544013989817001-dce138f6-6231-4650-8f7c-74ba36825e16"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f135e7d329a834a13aac15e197484513ad2fc3dc1d218d017ec323e9582413ab","event_uuid":"6d0188db-4e7a-432a-8296-3f1a3b6227ea","position":{"commit_sha":"07d851cc203add599b241e7368e4a531f78467d3","position":"1787544018225900001-6d0188db-4e7a-432a-8296-3f1a3b6227ea"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4e2decf4d5c0b480d94899f4b398ac38640342484809704b2a8e9ae49809aaa7","event_uuid":"fa510776-895d-402b-8881-1768006935a9","position":{"commit_sha":"ea09ff18e9e54a0fae6011e92187d20eff2294e6","position":"1787544585520900105-fa510776-895d-402b-8881-1768006935a9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Phase 1 RCA — completion-verifier faults verdict-less on epic-close transport read-timeout\n\n**Investigation:** 4 parallel investigators (code-tracer, historical, empirical runtime, pydantic-ai OSS lens). They **converge** on a single mechanism with an aggravating condition. Legitimacy: **`defect`** (resilience/bounding gap — cited below). Not a shared-store/contention issue.\n\n### Proven root cause (parsimonious — one defect + one aggravating condition)\n\nThe completion-verifier's `CompletionAgentStep.run` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:100-113`) routes into the banked/deterministic recovery **only** three *typed output/budget* exhaustion exceptions — `LLMBudgetExhaustedError`, `RunawayToolLoopError`, `UnretryableOutputError` (token exhaustion). A **transport-availability failure** matches none of them.\n\nOn the epic-close finalize step (`gates/completion-verification.yaml` `decide.then.verify`, `output_budget: model_max`), the single large `converse` call read-times-out. Its finite provider retries exhaust — botocore `max_attempts=4 × read_timeout=600s` on the Bedrock path (`bedrock_model.py:171-174`), or tenacity `stop_after_attempt(4) × httpx.Timeout(600)` on the Anthropic path — and the failure is wrapped as **`LLMUnavailableError`** at `run_failure.py:202`.\n\n`LLMUnavailableError(LLMError)` is a **sibling** of the caught `LLMRunnerError` subclasses (`errors.py:11,15,29,33,70`), so it is provably **not** caught by `run()`'s three `except` arms. It propagates past recovery to `completion_failures.py:232`, which raises the verdict-less `LLMError(\"completion verification workflow did not produce a verdict: …\")`. **The gate faults instead of degrading to a verdict.**\n\n- **Defect (the changeable artifact):** the missing transport-availability recovery arm at `completion_recovery.py:100-113` — an exhausted-provider `LLMUnavailableError` is never routed to the deterministic no-LLM finalizer.\n- **Aggravating condition (why the timeout occurs at all):** the epic finalize call is large — the PRIMARY step budget is scaled up by direct-child count (`completion.py:233-236`) and the finalize runs at `output_budget=model_max` — so the single `converse` reliably exceeds the 600s read timeout. (Note: the close path uses `graph=False` at `close_autoresume.py:237`, so this is *not* descendant-subtree concatenation; it is step-budget-scaled agent history.)\n\n### Proof (discriminating experiments + runtime oracle)\n\n- **Retry engages (disproves rival A \"retry not applied\").** Empirical dynamic probe: a `MockTransport` raising `ReadTimeout` on every call drove **4** transport attempts (backoff 1s/2s/4s) then re-raised. `interpret_failure(wrapped ReadTimeout)` → **`LLMUnavailableError`** (runtime-observed), which is not one of the three recovery-catchable types.\n- **Wall-clock arithmetic matches (supports B).** `4 × 600s (+backoff) = 2407s ≈ 40.1 min` — an exact match to the deterministic ~40 min, 3/3-identical reproduction.\n- **Deterministic, not transient infra (disproves rival D).** 3/3 identical ~40 min faults are structural (a large call that always exceeds 600s), not a variable infra blip. The class hierarchy makes the propagation deterministic.\n- **Timeout-too-low (rival C) is an aggravating/mitigating factor, not the cause** — even a higher timeout would still fault verdict-less, because the timeout bypasses recovery.\n\n### Authoritative intended-behavior source (clears the not-a-bug guard → `defect`)\n\n`completion_recovery.py:11-12` (module docstring): *\"…a deterministic no-LLM fallback so a run with any banked progress can never die verdict-less.\"* The banked-recovery design (epics 10ae / 2948) exists precisely so the gate **degrades to a verdict rather than faults**. The transport-timeout path violates that invariant. Severity is **availability, not correctness** — it fails closed (no false PASS), it just fails *verdict-less* instead of degrading to an actionable BLOCK/FAIL.\n\nIndependent OSS corroboration (pydantic-ai lens, P0): the idiomatic fix across every resilience pattern is to **catch the provider fault and emit an explicit degrade verdict** rather than let it propagate as a fault. (It also flags that a pure Bedrock-Converse path raises botocore `ReadTimeoutError`, not `httpx.ReadTimeout` — so the dossier's `failure.py:271` httpx `WAIT_AND_RETRY` arm is the wrong transport; but classification is advisory metadata only — nothing re-runs the decide step on it — so the fix is at the recovery-routing layer, not classification.)\n\n### Defect attribution (`caused_by`)\n\n**`caused_by = d2ce-36f5-fd08-4e40`** — commit `5bc3a432d7` \"d2ce: default local dev to Bedrock\" (epic 061c seam). Class: **regression**. Before this cutover, local gate calls ran on direct Anthropic, whose tenacity transport envelope (story arcticduck, `anthropic_model.py`) absorbed transient transport timeouts before they reached the gate. Switching the default gate provider to Bedrock removed that net without providing an equivalent gate-level degrade, so an exhausted transport timeout now escapes to the verdict-less fault. A reviewer of d2ce could plausibly have asked whether the Bedrock path had equivalent transient-timeout resilience — so it satisfies the \"reviewer could have caught this\" test.\n\n**Divergence note (per protocol):** a whole-file blame of the *fix site* (`completion_recovery.py` / `completion_failures.py`) would misattribute to the banked-recovery story `9a08`/`dcc90`, which is the fix site, not the cause site (date test: `dcc90` 2026-07-27 predates the fault becoming reachable at `d2ce` 2026-08-04). `9a08` deliberately scoped recovery to *typed* exhaustion; it was `d2ce` that made the transport-timeout path escape verdict-less. Confidence **MODERATE**: the deeper \"gate-level degrade for any transport failure\" obligation was arguably never owned by a single ticket; `61d8` later added botocore retries to Bedrock (partial remediation) yet the fault persists, confirming the residual defect is at the decide-step/gate degrade layer. If one ticket must carry it, it is `d2ce`.\n\n### Chronic-area context\n\nGate resilience here is demonstrably chronic (46a2→3211 \"incomplete fix\" tool-loop; 0707 banking follow-on defect; 12b7 sharding won't-fix; 10ae context rework; 61d8 inert Bedrock retry knobs; a live cluster of OPEN `llm-degrade` session_logs across all three gates). The recurring theme: **gates fail closed to an un-actionable \"could not run\" instead of degrading to a verdict.** This fix targets the transport-timeout instance of that theme.\n\n### Fix direction (Phase 2)\n\nRoute an exhausted-provider `LLMUnavailableError` from the PRIMARY verify run into a **deterministic degrade** — finalize from the criterion bank via the existing no-LLM finalizer (honoring \"can never die verdict-less\"), *without* launching more (also-timing-out) LLM successor runs; when the bank is empty, emit a deterministic fail-closed verdict carrying a provider-unavailable finding. RED→GREEN with a held-out oracle + defect-seeded mutation.","timestamp":1787537967247576001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RCA — CORRECTED (supersedes the earlier comment; ultrathink + runtime experiments)\n\n**Observed failure:** epic REB-3233 (3d7a-7795) close ran the completion verifier ~40 min, 3/3, then\nfaulted \"completion verification workflow did not produce a verdict\" with **exit 1** (hard,\nnon-retryable, offers `--force`).\n\n**Earlier RCA framings were WRONG (recorded so they are not re-tried):**\n- *\"Missing degrade arm → fabricate a deterministic verdict\"* — rejected: that verdict is\n  `certifiable=False`; close_precheck.py:696-704 would then close the ticket WITHOUT a certified\n  signature, violating the certified-close requirement and MASKING the real defect.\n- *\"600s per-call timeout too low for a large epic (scale it up)\"* — rejected by runtime\n  experiment: in a healthy Bedrock window the epic's converse calls run **~11s each**\n  (`llm_ms 361s / 32 requests`), none near 600s, and the verify COMPLETES a `certifiable=true`\n  PASS. So 600s is ample under normal conditions; the 3/3 ~40-min faults were a **sustained\n  Bedrock-slowness window** (a transient provider availability event), not a structural >600s call.\n- *caused_by = d2ce (Bedrock-default cutover)* — WITHDRAWN: the exit-1-vs-exit-11 defect is\n  **provider-independent** (it drops the disposition for ANY retryable outage), so the Bedrock\n  cutover is not its origin.\n\n**PROVEN root cause (provider-independent, structural):** a retryable provider outage that occurs\nMID-RUN in the completion gate surfaces as a **non-retryable exit-1 hard fault instead of the\nexit-11 \"transient — retry\"** the gate posture was designed to produce.\n- `close_precheck.py:629-631` is the exit-11 consumer: `_outcome = failure.outcome_of(exc);\n  _rc = 11 if (_outcome and _outcome.retryable) else 1`.\n- The classifier DOES compute the retryable disposition and attach it to the raised\n  `LLMUnavailableError` (`run_failure.py:174 provider_err.outcome = outcome`).\n- BUT the mid-run completion outage is stringified into a `RunResult.error` at the workflow-executor\n  boundary (`executor.py` StepResult/RunResult carry `error: str`, not the exception), and\n  `raise_completion_workflow_failure` (completion_failures.py:231 / the CompletionRecoveryError\n  raises in completion_recovery.py) raises a **fresh `LLMError`/`CompletionRecoveryError` with NO\n  `.outcome`** → `outcome_of(exc)` returns `None` → `_rc = 1`.\n- **Parity proof:** the plan-review gate does NOT have this bug — `plan_review_recovery.py`\n  `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (story authorial-hated-blackbear) does\n  `outcome = failure.outcome_of(error)` then `**failure.resolution_fields(outcome)` so a retryable\n  outage maps to exit 11. The completion gate was left on \"Shape B (raised error)\" but its mid-run\n  raise path never attaches `.outcome`.\n\n**Discriminating evidence:**\n- Healthy-window full epic verify (REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT=1200, 1 attempt): **COMPLETED, verdict PASS,\n  certifiable=true**, 10 criteria, 32 requests, ~11s/call — disproves the \"structural >600s\" and\n  \"infra-broken\" rivals and confirms the fault was a transient slowness window.\n- Small-leaf Bedrock health probe: PASS certifiable=true in 140s — Bedrock healthy.\n- Code trace: `failure.outcome_of` (failure.py:550) reads `getattr(error,\"outcome\",None)` — it does\n  NOT re-classify; the raised error MUST carry `.outcome`, and the mid-run completion path does not.\n\n**Defect attribution (caused_by = authorial-hated-blackbear / commit 3938c7ed2d60, epic jira-reb-687):**\nthat story (\"two-scope gate posture — exit 11, disposition plumbing\") built the exit-11 CONSUMER for\nthe completion gate (`_completion_precheck` raises 11 on a retryable `.outcome`) and wired the\nPRODUCER for the plan-review/code-review \"Shape A\" degraded-verdict paths, but never wired the\ncompletion gate's mid-run \"Shape B\" raise path to ATTACH `.outcome`. Consumer added, producer\nomitted, within the one integrator story — an incomplete implementation of its own design. Class:\nplan_defect. (Secondary: `failure._map` has an httpx-timeout retryable arm but no botocore arm — a\nprovider-parity gap that determines whether a Bedrock read-timeout is retryable at first\nclassification; folded into the fix for robustness.)\n\n**Fix (mirror the blackbear plan-review pattern in the completion gate):** forward the retryable\ndisposition from the primary/recovery exception's `.outcome` onto the error raised by\n`raise_completion_workflow_failure`, so `outcome_of(exc)` returns retryable and close_precheck exits\n11 \"transient — retry\" (never uncertified-closes, never fabricates a verdict). Plus add the\nbotocore/provider-agnostic read-timeout arm to `failure._map` for parity with httpx.","timestamp":1787541837887253001}],"created_at":1787536885733823001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dae3802c-b3ab-4d01-b2d5-215bca27c592","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"},{"link_uuid":"9f301206-75af-4db1-8594-578c28cf8a95","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"d2ce-36f5-fd08-4e40"},{"link_uuid":"fa510776-895d-402b-8881-1768006935a9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9620-1598-fc27-41e4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nClosing a large epic runs the completion-verifier close gate, whose final\n`decide@then/verify` step makes an LLM (Bedrock `converse`) call. On epic\n`3d7a-7795-efde-4df7` (REB-3233, 13 children) the gate ran ~40 minutes and then\nFAULTED — it produced **neither PASS nor FAIL/BLOCK**, but an error:\n\n```\ncannot close 3d7a-7795-efde-4df7: completion verification could not run\n(completion verification workflow did not produce a verdict:\n step 'decide@then/verify' failed: the LLM provider call failed:\n Read timeout on endpoint URL:\n \"https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/model/us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6/converse\").\n```\n\nThis is a fault in the gate itself: a transient/among-oversized provider Read\ntimeout is surfaced as \"could not run / no verdict\", so a legitimate close cannot\ncomplete without `--force`. Reproduced deterministically: three consecutive close\nattempts on this epic all faulted identically (~40+ min each, EXIT 1).\n\n`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:271` classifies `httpx.ReadTimeout`\n(`httpx.TimeoutException`) as `WAIT_AND_RETRY`, and `config.py` documents a retry\npolicy over transient timeouts — yet the gate still terminated with no verdict via\n`completion_failures.py:232` (\"... did not produce a verdict\"). So either the\nverifier's decide-step path does not apply the retry, retries are exhausted because\neach attempt sends an oversized accumulated context that itself read-times-out, or\nthe effective per-request timeout is too low for a large-AC epic-close verification.\n\nThis defect class has rich history (verifier sharding `12b7`, banked/resumable AC\nverification `2948`, context reworks `10ae`, step-budget loops `46a2`/`3211`,\n`REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT` wiring `02cd`, Bedrock provider seam+timeout `061c`, gates\nrunning minutes-scale `1e88`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A transient provider Read timeout during the completion verifier's\n  `decide@then/verify` step no longer terminates the gate with \"could not run / no\n  verdict\"; it is handled per the WAIT_AND_RETRY classification (bounded retry) OR\n  the verification work is bounded so a single call cannot exceed the provider read\n  timeout — root cause to be confirmed by /rebar-debug before the fix. Proven by a\n  RED→GREEN test that exercises the confirmed mechanism.\n- [ ] A large-epic close (many children / large AC set) completes through the gate\n  without a raw provider read-timeout fault, or degrades to an actionable verdict\n  rather than an un-actionable \"could not run\".\n\n## Testing\n\n- [ ] A unit/integration test reproduces the faulting path (verifier decide step\n  raising `httpx.ReadTimeout`) and asserts the post-fix behavior (bounded retry\n  and/or bounded context / actionable outcome), seen RED before the fix and GREEN\n  after, with a mutation check.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9620-1598-fc27-41e4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"dce138f6-6231-4650-8f7c-74ba36825e16","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8c8a-2756-ecfa-4b90","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion-verifier close gate faults (no verdict) on a Bedrock Read timeout during decide@then/verify for large-epic closes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dd20981a-22c8-46a3-b392-8ed89f659f6c","dae3802c-b3ab-4d01-b2d5-215bca27c592","7d5e0bbd-e8fc-4c0a-bf63-39f278432907","9f301206-75af-4db1-8594-578c28cf8a95","bc900acc-24fc-43db-9400-3a89c7a395e9","dce138f6-6231-4650-8f7c-74ba36825e16","6d0188db-4e7a-432a-8296-3f1a3b6227ea","fa510776-895d-402b-8881-1768006935a9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787548164348089001,"uuid":"d4e614dd-52b3-4bf9-aadf-b142410ce15c"}